WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.998 --> 00:00:08.099
&gt;&gt;&gt; Want to bring back our

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:09.534
political experts for more

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:10.702
analysis on the breaking news

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:11.903
we're following now.

00:00:12.036 --> 00:00:14.939
Ron Desantis officially publicly

00:00:15.073 --> 00:00:17.342
launching his campaign for

00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:18.076
president of the United States

00:00:18.209 --> 00:00:19.744
on Twitter.

00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:20.712
I understand they've got some

00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:22.881
problems over there.

00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:23.448
What are you hearing?

00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:24.716
&gt;&gt; Yeah, this was a concern some

00:00:24.716 --> 00:00:25.784
people had today when they said

00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:26.885
they were going to be announcing

00:00:27.018 --> 00:00:30.789
this on Twitter spaces, which is

00:00:30.922 --> 00:00:33.558
this audio only offer Twitter

00:00:33.691 --> 00:00:34.826
has where you can go and list

00:00:34.959 --> 00:00:39.230
ton a conversation someone has.

00:00:39.364 --> 00:00:41.866
Clearly I'm not sure if they

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.734
anticipated how many people

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.402
would be listening or trying to

00:00:44.736 --> 00:00:45.170
join.

00:00:45.303 --> 00:00:46.304
Obviously quite a audience on

00:00:46.738 --> 00:00:47.738
this.

00:00:46.738 --> 00:00:47.872
There's a lot of glitching that

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:50.241
are delaying this.

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:51.643
It's still difficult to listen

00:00:51.776 --> 00:00:52.744
to this.

00:00:52.777 --> 00:00:54.212
It's not clear if it's fully

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:54.746
started.

00:00:54.746 --> 00:00:58.049
They were trying to do so a few

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.250
moments ago.

00:00:59.384 --> 00:01:00.752
You heard Elon Musk briefly

00:01:00.885 --> 00:01:03.354
speaking on this, but it kept

00:01:03.488 --> 00:01:05.423
crashing and dropping.

00:01:05.557 --> 00:01:06.891
This is something that was a

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:07.725
potential to happen.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:09.093
Obviously Twitter has not been

00:01:09.227 --> 00:01:10.762
running smoothly as you've seen

00:01:10.762 --> 00:01:12.030
how understaffed it's been and

00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:13.798
even the Biden campaign has been

00:01:13.932 --> 00:01:15.066
mocking it already.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:15.867
President Biden sending out a

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.468
tweet saying this link works.

00:01:17.602 --> 00:01:19.270
It's a link to fund raise for

00:01:19.404 --> 00:01:21.439
his campaign.

00:01:21.573 --> 00:01:22.774
He's already ribbing the

00:01:22.774 --> 00:01:24.342
Desantis campaign launch and

00:01:24.776 --> 00:01:25.910
just how glitchy it is.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.579
Not off to a smooth start.

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:28.813
This is the concern of course

00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:30.782
and this is what when you have

00:01:30.782 --> 00:01:31.816
those similar traditional

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:32.951
campaign announcements, you

00:01:33.084 --> 00:01:34.786
don't have an issue like this,

00:01:34.919 --> 00:01:36.921
but this is how the Desantis

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:38.990
campaign so far is getting

00:01:39.123 --> 00:01:39.324
started.

00:01:39.457 --> 00:01:41.326
Where they're having not a very

00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:43.561
controlled issue and Elon Musk

00:01:43.695 --> 00:01:45.630
keeps talking about how many

00:01:45.763 --> 00:01:47.131
people are trying to listen.

00:01:47.265 --> 00:01:48.900
The expectation is that they

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.802
knew it would be a widely

00:01:50.802 --> 00:01:52.237
listened to campaign launch and

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.938
clearly it's having a lot of

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:54.272
issues.

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:55.807
I don't even think it's

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:56.174
happening.

00:01:56.307 --> 00:01:57.742
&gt;&gt; It's very awkward.

00:01:57.876 --> 00:01:59.344
It was supposed to start about

00:01:59.477 --> 00:02:00.812
20 minutes or so ago.

00:02:00.812 --> 00:02:02.814
Hasn't started yet.

00:02:02.814 --> 00:02:05.316
Sarah, you're our social media

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:05.650
analyst.

00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:11.856
You're an expert in this area.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:15.026
Give us your analysis of this

00:02:15.159 --> 00:02:15.460
major glitch.

00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:19.097
&gt;&gt; I was in that audio space and

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.134
when I joined, there were about

00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:25.003
667,000 people trying to listen.

00:02:25.136 --> 00:02:27.171
Twitter has held much bigger

00:02:27.305 --> 00:02:27.505
events.

00:02:27.639 --> 00:02:29.641
When Elon did his bbc interview

00:02:29.774 --> 00:02:31.109
through audio, I think that got

00:02:31.242 --> 00:02:35.413
up to 3 million people but what

00:02:35.546 --> 00:02:37.248
I think they didn't anticipate

00:02:37.382 --> 00:02:38.349
was that many people coming in

00:02:38.483 --> 00:02:39.751
at the same time.

00:02:39.884 --> 00:02:40.852
Because they said it would start

00:02:40.852 --> 00:02:42.487
at 6:00, over a million people

00:02:42.854 --> 00:02:44.088
trying to listen to this.

00:02:44.222 --> 00:02:46.291
And the problem is that when you

00:02:46.424 --> 00:02:47.892
have such a high frequency event

00:02:48.026 --> 00:02:49.894
in any kind of technology.

00:02:50.028 --> 00:02:55.266
On social media, I'm on my phone

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:55.533
now.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:56.534
It can be in streaming.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:03:00.905
It's the huge amount of people

00:03:01.039 --> 00:03:01.539
that often messes this up.

00:03:01.673 --> 00:03:03.274
The problem is that he's trying

00:03:03.408 --> 00:03:05.076
to send this message that I can

00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:06.544
bypass the traditional media.

00:03:06.878 --> 00:03:08.880
Go direct to my listeners.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.481
Well, when the first time you

00:03:10.882 --> 00:03:12.450
try to do that in launching your

00:03:12.884 --> 00:03:14.452
campaign, it doesn't work and

00:03:14.886 --> 00:03:23.361
you're almost a half hour late

00:03:23.494 --> 00:03:24.429
to your announcement.

00:03:24.562 --> 00:03:25.096
&gt;&gt; This is clearly not the

00:03:25.229 --> 00:03:25.797
rollout that Desantis and his

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:26.431
campaign were looking for.

00:03:26.564 --> 00:03:27.098
Or hoping for, is it?

00:03:27.231 --> 00:03:27.999
&gt;&gt; No, it's not.

00:03:28.132 --> 00:03:29.233
But I mean, I think we have to

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:40.912
be honest that this outcome

00:03:40.912 --> 00:03:42.180
pretty predictable.

00:03:42.313 --> 00:03:43.781
The challenge with doing an

00:03:43.915 --> 00:03:45.249
event like this and you're

00:03:45.383 --> 00:03:48.519
trying to present an image of a

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:49.320
competent campaign that knows

00:03:49.454 --> 00:03:51.189
how to put together a smooth

00:03:51.322 --> 00:03:56.194
running event, which is a

00:03:56.327 --> 00:03:59.097
microcosm of a smooth running

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.932
campaign, doing it in this

00:04:00.932 --> 00:04:01.666
format introduced a huge amount

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:02.400
of risk.

00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:03.434
What's happening now is that

00:04:03.568 --> 00:04:05.169
instead of talking about what

00:04:05.303 --> 00:04:08.239
Ron Desantis is running on and

00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:12.410
how he's running, what his

00:04:12.543 --> 00:04:13.378
campaign looks like, people are

00:04:13.511 --> 00:04:15.380
going to be talking about how

00:04:15.513 --> 00:04:16.147
this event went.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.482
There's such a thing as negative

00:04:17.615 --> 00:04:18.983
attention and right now, getting

00:04:19.417 --> 00:04:22.120
a lot of negative attention and

00:04:22.253 --> 00:04:22.954
it's probably going to continue

00:04:22.987 --> 00:04:23.588
and it's probably not going to

00:04:23.721 --> 00:04:24.989
be undone by anything that is

00:04:25.123 --> 00:04:26.557
said later tonight in a more

00:04:26.958 --> 00:04:30.962
traditional format.

00:04:30.962 --> 00:04:32.964
First impressions matter a lot

00:04:32.964 --> 00:04:33.498
in politics.

00:04:33.631 --> 00:04:34.966
I think he is learning a really

00:04:34.966 --> 00:04:36.300
important lesson right now that

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:40.038
you know, if you're going to do

00:04:40.171 --> 00:04:40.972
something unconventional, you

00:04:40.972 --> 00:04:41.806
have to have your ducks in a row

00:04:41.939 --> 00:04:42.974
and understand how this is

00:04:42.974 --> 00:04:44.976
working and as Sarah was saying,

00:04:44.976 --> 00:04:47.612
there are about 600,000 people

00:04:47.745 --> 00:04:48.980
in this event.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.415
That's not actually that many

00:04:50.548 --> 00:04:50.982
people.

00:04:50.982 --> 00:04:52.383
When I checked a couple of

00:04:52.517 --> 00:04:54.018
minutes ago, it was about

00:04:54.152 --> 00:04:55.920
300,000.

00:04:56.054 --> 00:04:56.654
So a lot of people are leaving.

00:04:56.988 --> 00:04:58.423
Maybe they're being kicked out

00:04:58.556 --> 00:05:02.427
because of technical glitches.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:09.367
Those are not huge numbers.

